  message: "F3 LANDED THE SCHEME BUMP; STATUS LEFT OPEN (todo_hard) because the post-merge live check found the v9 contract unmet in 7 languages (INV-punig, isbefore this item). Owner decision needed there.\n\nPR #1571, merge 3c9f03a81f (rebase; B5/B7/B8a hunks + F1 + F2 + F3): STABLE_ID_SCHEME hypergumbo-stableid-v8 -> v9; spec version-history entry (contract: every repeatable enclosing scope hashed, no line numbers/ordinals, repo-relative paths, declared arity + Ada result type, every kind; churn per language; enforcement; migration), ADR-0035 Status + §5 gate contract + §6 \"Follow-on v8 -> v9\", CHANGELOG Changed section with a consumer migration note. F3 in-campaign fixes: containment linker roots dotted names no phase placed at their file (corpus: dotted orphans 388 -> 5, +383 contains edges, 0 removed; the renamed Lean structs, Lean/F# namespaced functions, C++ out-of-line methods, dotted modules, HCL var.X), never makes a file a child, and requires a Phase-1.5 owner in the child's file carrying the prefix as its qualified name; Racket/Scheme param_count = len(meta.parameters) + signature as written (not an id input: 0 ids changed); C#/TypeScript/Tcl names carry every enclosing namespace (C# 70/316 sample qualified_names; a C# property under nested same-name namespaces tied and now does not). PR #1572, merge fa502d7d75: Solidity libraries minted no id and rode the floor (5 on the OpenZeppelin sample, the only floor ids on three samples; the gate fixture had no library) -> overload_arity.scoped_stable_id, no bump. Cache: the results-cache key hashes every hypergumbo .py file (analyzer_identity), so v8 entries are not served.\n\nEVIDENCE (merged dev, `hypergumbo run --include-docs`, earlier sibling blanked, survivors by (kind,name,line,col); scratchpad fixes/f3/live/): C-family cpp 3/3, JVM java 4/4, .NET csharp namespaces 3/3, ML ocaml 4/4, Lisp racket 2/2 + clojure 4/4, BEAM elixir 3/3, IDL proto 8/8, config ini 3/3, shell bash 3/3, web vue 1/1 + twig 3/3, Ada result-type overloads 3/3, INV-fabih scala 4/4 kotlin 4/4 csharp 5/5 swift 4/4: same id, 0 moved, 0 null. Filed shape (same-file overloads): cuda 2/2, glsl 2/2, julia 2/2, erlang 3/3, csharp indexers 3/3, nim 2/2 same, 0 null. Same-scope ties move as ADR-0035 §1 accepts (a second top-level `# Intro`; two `{% macro input %}` in one template, illegal Twig). Corpus validation_report.stable_id_stats on dev fa502d7d75: code sample 24,670 nodes / 68 languages, config 5,903 / 36, extra 1,322 / 9: floor_cohort 0, floor_abstained 0, none_cohort 0, collisions 0 in all three; checkout-location: 0 of 21,168 / 5,704 / 1,262 positions differ when the same files are analyzed from a deeper, differently named directory. Gate: 152 fixtures, both baseline sections empty (full targeted run 25,079 passed).\n\nNOT MET (INV-punig): a same-name construct under two different parents moves when the first parent is deleted in markdown (sections, code blocks), rst (sections), scss (nested rules), puppet (resources in classes), svelte (template blocks), apex (nested classes), fish (nested functions); mermaid repeats a node id across subgraphs (may be one node). Also filed: perl block packages misname subs (WI-himah), ocaml call bound to a type (WI-dibiv), V one-letter type alias (WI-fuzaj), solidity structs not emitted (WI-fuvit), file-node spans shorter than their declarations (INV-palot), python nested-class qualified_name (WI-naviz)."  # 867a
