  message: "DONE. PRs: #1558 (B1 gate + arity helper), #1559 (B2), #1560 (B3), #1562 (B4), #1563 (B5), #1565 (B6), #1566 (B7), #1570 (B8a), #1571 (THE scheme bump v8 -> v9), #1572, #1575, #1576 (F4: INV-punig, every producer hashes its parent + two-parent guard; merge 1997a56d0d), #1577 (Perl block packages + SPARQL ordinals; 4d5a8ec889), #1578 (docs counts; e315bcb5b9). Blocker INV-punig is satisfied. All value changes are inside v9 (unreleased).\nACCEPTANCE, condition by condition (evidence on dev 4d5a8ec889 unless noted):\n(A) original: \"per language, the producer computes the ADR-0035 formula (with a test that two same-name overloads in one file get ids that do not depend on emission order), or a written verdict\" -> HOLDS. test_stable_id_floor_gate.py: 204 fixtures, each with an earlier same-name sibling (overload, clause, same-name in another scope), census floor_and_null EMPTY for every kind and language, sibling_deletion_moves EMPTY. Overload shape live (CLI, F3 tusad_orig.py on 1997a56d0d): cuda 2/2, glsl 2/2, julia 2/2, erlang 3/3, csharp indexers 3/3, nim 2/2 same, 0 null.\n(B) owner (1) every producer that rode the WI-motiz floor computes the producer formula, incl. 0-floor languages -> HOLDS: census empty on the fixtures (every kind, include_docs); corpus validation_report.stable_id_stats floor_cohort 0 on code (24,670 nodes / 68 langs), config (5,903 / 36), extra (1,322 / 9).\n(C) owner (2) one shared arity helper -> HOLDS: overload_arity.declared_arity / declared_arity_stable_id (+ node_declared_arity_stable_id, scoped_stable_id, scoped_table_stable_id, pass_minted_stable_id built on it).\n(D) owner (3a) null is a failure via a per-language shrink-only baseline ratcheted to 0 -> HOLDS: .ci/stable-id-floor-baseline.json both sections empty; growth and unrecorded shrink fail; corpus none_cohort 0 and floor_abstained 0 on all three samples (not one sample alone).\n(E) owner (3b) cross-language delete-an-earlier-sibling test, no other id moves -> HOLDS for every shape the gate holds, and the gate now proves the two-parent shape per language: test_every_language_has_a_two_parent_fixture_or_is_flat (96 two-parent fixtures; 24 FLAT languages with reasons, stale-checked) + test_every_registered_language_has_a_fixture. Live CLI (first parent / sibling blanked, survivors matched one by one on (kind,name,line,col)): all 96 two-parent + else + maven fixtures 365/365 same on 1997a56d0d; perl-blocks 3/3 and sparql-queries 2/2 on 4d5a8ec889; F3 family table re-run: cpp 3/3, java 4/4, csharp-namespaces 3/3, ocaml 4/4, racket 2/2, clojure 4/4, elixir 3/3, proto 8/8, ini 3/3, bash 3/3, vue 1/1, Ada result-type 3/3, INV-fabih scala 4/4 kotlin 4/4 csharp 5/5 swift 4/4; INV-fabih original probe 0 moved in 6 languages.\n(F) \"do not close on none_cohort alone\" -> closure rests on (A)-(E), not on none_cohort.\nSTILL MOVING, by ADR-0035 §1 design (same-scope ties ordered by the per-file split pass; not two-parent cases): a second top-level `# Intro` heading, two `{% macro input %}` in one Twig template, a Mermaid node id repeated in two subgraphs (one Mermaid node).\nCHECKOUT LOCATION: 0 of 21,168 / 5,704 / 1,262 positions differ between two checkouts.\nNOT CHECKED: Apex and Puppet on real code (no corpus files; fixtures only); languages outside the 104 the gate covers (registry check: only yaml, html, play-routes lack a fixture, with reasons).\nFILED from F4: WI-budoh (ansible tasks as handler), WI-vazab (robot *** Tasks ***), WI-raduj (play-routes sub-project routes not found under run), WI-bodug (verilog tasks/functions not emitted). Ledger: scratchpad fixes/tusad/TUSAD_PLAN.md F4 line."  # 96e4
